From ffa738dd3e3dd2fc44b78bf0340b0da9b73ec0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahdiotllfer <ahdiotllfer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] devices: Add virtio-gpu device (2D + venus via virglrenderer)
virtio-gpu paravirtual display: 2D scanout, EDID, cursor, multi-scanout,
plus optional venus 3D acceleration hosted by virglrenderer (dlopen'd at
runtime). On iOS virglrenderer is built against MoltenVK (Vulkan over
Metal); any host Vulkan driver works elsewhere.

Venus plumbing: virgl/venus capsets, contexts (CONTEXT_INIT), 3D
resources, blob resources with a host-visible SHM window exposed through
the virtio-mmio SHM registers, transfers, and deferred fence completion
so guests never observe SUBMIT_3D completion before rendering ends.

Blobs are mapped at guest-chosen window offsets via direct-map MMIO
regions; SET_SCANOUT_BLOB blits mapped blobs into display VRAM.
